              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Stephen R. McCallister, the petitioner argues that voluntary statements obtained in violation of constitutional standards may be used for impeachment when the defendant testifies at trial."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Nicole A. Saharsky",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b094e89ff63a-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 14,
                "start": 14
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Nicole A. Saharsky, the petitioner (through amicus counsel) contends that the rule allowing such statements for impeachment should apply in this case."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MS. SAHARSKY",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b094e89ff63a-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 20,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MS. SAHARSKY, the petitioner argues that excluding the evidence would impose a strong price on the government, citing prior cases such as Havens, Walder, Harris, Hass, and Harvey."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Stephen R. McAllister",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b094e89ff63a3a9fc73115dc219cfdfe6097571ba864151d857ca2463d066afc",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b094e89ff63a-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Stephen R. McAllister, the petitioner argues that the balancing of interests in Sixth Amendment cases is a modest consideration, referencing Nix v. Williams and Michigan v. Harvey."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Kansas (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
